    "description": "Samaria, the capital of the northern kingdom of Israel, was conquered by the Assyrian king Shalmaneser V (r. 726-722 BC), probably in 722 BC. The city and the area around it, were reorganized into an Assyrian province.",
    "details": "<p><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-58955546-7fff-5ab3-b316-ff915865c5a8\">The province is mentioned in an administrative text dating to the reign of Sargon II (r. 721-705). Two of its governors held the position of <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://www.ucl.ac.uk/sargon/eponymlistsandchronicles/\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">eponym</a>: once during the reign of Sennacherib (690 BC) and once in the time of Ashurbanipal (after 648 BC). A governor of the province of Samaria is mentioned in a seventh-century-BC legal transaction of the Assyrian royal court.</span></p>",
